    "narrative": "For May 11, 2026, the Zurich Zebras\u2019 lineup is anchored by **Junior Caminero** (67.23) and **Yordan Alvarez** (64.21), who represent our strongest offensive engines. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a favorable matchup against Kevin Gausman, as his dynamic platoon profile and high-leverage spot in the two-hole outweigh the SP\u2019s moderate xERA. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start despite facing George Kirby; his elite xwOBA (0.429) provides the necessary floor to overcome the SP\u2019s skill, while his placement in the order bolsters his run-production potential. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) rounds out the high-tier projections, capitalizing on a significant boost from an exploitable 5.30 xERA against Roki Sasaki, where his R-handed platoon edge drives his score well above his base expectation.\n\nManaging the fringe of our lineup remains a delicate balance as we navigate a day where our high-speed depth, including **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, and **Caleb Durbin**, is largely sidelined by off-days. Consequently, **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.61) and **Luke Raley** (52.38) are forced into the mix. **Kazuma Okamoto** faces the stiffest challenge against Drew Rasmussen; while his raw power is high, the SP\u2019s 3.67 xERA and a negative platoon split depress his ceiling. **Hyeseong Kim** (41.19) is the most precarious start, sitting barely above the floor; his value is severely compressed by a tough matchup against Trevor McDonald (2.60 xERA) and an unfavorable eighth-order slot, though his defensive profile keeps him active over bench alternatives like **Colt Keith** or **Zac Veen**. \n\nWith **Christian Yelich** remaining sidelined on the IL, our roster flexibility is limited today. All decisions are currently subject to the \"Lineup Pending\" tag; while we have modeled our expectations on historical placement, any late shift moving **Kazuma Okamoto** or **Hyeseong Kim** further down the batting order will necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their efficiency scores to ensure we aren't burning daily caps on sub-40 performances. We continue to monitor the status of depth pieces like **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** to ensure we are prepared for any mid-game substitutions if weather or late-scratch announcements compromise our starters.",
